        "layout": "rich_text",
        "heading": "ABOUT THE COURSE",
        "heading_style": "section",
        "text": "<p><strong>Certified Professional Groomer (CPG) </strong> </p><p>Class size: &nbsp;Maximum 6 students</p><p><strong>Items included in All ICMG courses:</strong></p><ul><li>Text books and student login portal where your instructor will review all that you have completed.&nbsp;</li><li>Grooming Uniform</li><li>Grooming Kit</li><li>Exam fees</li><li>Those who pass the course have an opportunity to work in our salon and gain paid salon experience which is invaluable on your CV</li></ul><p><strong>Stage 1 Examination: Bath and Dry </strong></p><p>This qualification is designed to help learners understand the roles and responsibilities of a professional dog groomer and the requirements for offering grooming services to clients.Learners will be required to demonstrate practical skills in:</p><ul><li>Safe handling and restraint</li><li>Effective bathing and drying of a coated breed</li><li>Hygiene area care</li><li>Nail trimming </li></ul><p><strong>Knowledge and understanding will cover: </strong></p><ul><li>Animal Welfare Legislation and Codes of Practice</li><li>Canine Health and Disease</li><li>Groomer Wellbeing </li></ul><p><strong>Assessment: </strong></p><ul><li>Practical Exam: Bath and Dry (Duration: 1 hour; Pass mark: 86% or above)</li><li>Written Exam: 100 questions (Duration: 1 hour)</li><li>Open Book: Pass mark 92% or above</li><li>Non-Open Book: Pass mark 86% or above</li></ul><p><strong>Assessement Requirements: </strong></p><ul><li>All dogs used for assessment must have a minimum&nbsp;at least 8 preferably 10&nbsp;weeks of fur&nbsp;growth.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>A comprehensive resource manual is provided, covering both practical and written exam content, including: </p><ul><li>Canine Handling and Behaviour</li><li>Skin and Hair Anatomy</li><li>Bathing and Drying Techniques</li><li>Canine Health and Diseases</li><li>Parasites and First Aid</li><li>Sanitation and Disinfection</li><li>Groomer Health and Safety </li></ul> <p><strong>Stage 2 Examination: Kennel/Pet Trim</strong></p><p>This advanced qualification builds on the foundational skills from Stage 1 and expands the learner’s understanding of pet grooming techniques, with a focus on pet or kennel trims.</p><p><strong>Learners will be required to demonstrate practical skills in: </strong></p><ul><li>Safe handling and restraint</li><li>Clipping and styling for a pet or kennel trim</li><li>Proficient use of clippers, blades, and scissors </li></ul><p><strong>Knowledge and understanding will cover: </strong></p><ul><li>Animal Welfare and Handling (including aggressive dogs)</li><li>Chemical safety</li><li>Dog handling and care</li><li>Skin anatomy, hair growth, and epidermal structures</li><li>Emergency procedures and groomer liability</li></ul><p><strong>Assessment: </strong></p><ul><li>Practical Exam: Kennel/Pet Trim (Duration: 1 hour; Pass mark: 86% or above)</li><li>Written Exam: 100 questions (Duration: 1 hour)</li><li>Open Book: Pass mark 92% or above</li><li>Non-Open Book: Pass mark 86% or above </li></ul><p><strong>Topics include: </strong></p><ul><li>Pet/Kennel Trimming Techniques</li><li>Handling Aggressive Dogs</li><li>Dog Grooming Importance</li><li>Skin Layers and Appendages (e.g., hair follicles, erector pili muscle)</li><li>Equipment Use and Maintenance (clippers, blades, scissors, comb attachments)</li><li>Emergency Response</li><li>Legal and Professional Responsibilities</li></ul><p>Note: All written exam questions are taken directly from the provided study guides. Answer formats include True/False and Multiple Choice.</p>",
